Now append the device-specific I2C + sensor config with the `on_value` automation (via printf `%.1f` translation
Let me reconsider the on_value implementation. The skill insists the observable must not be printed until a non-NaN value is published. A `logger.log` automation could fire on a transient NaN publish. I'll guard with an `isnan` check in a lambda, matching the skill's ESP_LOGx format-trans
← Edit artifacts/tmp102/prompt2c/tmp102.yaml
Index: /home/pi/Developer/wokwi-ai/artifacts/tmp102/prompt2c/tmp102.yaml
===================================================================
--- /home/pi/Developer/wokwi-ai/artifacts/tmp102/prompt2c/tmp102.yaml
+++ /home/pi/Developer/wokwi-ai/artifacts/tmp102/prompt2c/tmp102.yaml
@@ -30,10 +30,10 @@
 address: 0x48
 update_interval: 60s
 on_value:
   then:
-    - logger.log:
-        format: "Temperature = %.1f C"
-        args: ['x']
+    - lambda: !lambda |-
+        if (isnan(x)) return;
+        ESP_LOGI("tmp102", "Temperature = %.1f C", x);
 
 
 


